cff-version: 1.2.0
message: "If you use redrob-eval or a dataset generated with redrob-generate, please cite it as below."
title: "redrob-eval: an open LLM evaluation workbench with contamination-resistant generated tasks"
abstract: >-
  An open evaluation workbench for large language models. Compare models from any source on your
  own task, settle quality by blind human preference, evolve configurations under a quality floor,
  and serve self-hosted models. The Generate module produces evaluation items parametrically from
  content-derived seeds and scores them with deterministic verifiers, so a published set can be
  regenerated and audited by a third party rather than taken on trust.
type: software
authors:
  - family-names: Lee
    given-names: Janghoon
    alias: "이장훈"
version: 0.2.1
date-released: "2026-08-13"
license: Apache-2.0
repository-code: "https://github.com/redrob-labs/redrob-eval"
url: "https://github.com/redrob-labs/redrob-eval"
keywords:
  - large language models
  - evaluation
  - benchmark contamination
  - verifiable tasks
  - tokenizer fertility
# No `doi:` key yet: a Zenodo record has not been minted. It is deliberately absent rather than
# set to a placeholder, because the CFF schema requires a real `10.x` DOI there and a
# plausible-looking one that resolves to nothing is worse than none. Generated manifests carry
# `"doi": "TBD"` in their citation block for the same reason, so a shared dataset says plainly
# that its identifier is not final. Tracked in docs/decisions/0001-generate-foundation.md.
identifiers:
  - type: other
    value: "TBD"
    description: >-
      Placeholder for the Zenodo DOI, to be minted at first release.
references:
  - type: article
    title: "GEPA: Reflective Prompt Evolution Can Outperform Reinforcement Learning"
    year: 2025
    authors:
      - name: "Agrawal et al."
    identifiers:
      - type: other
        value: "arXiv:2507.19457"
        description: arXiv preprint
    notes: >-
      The Evolve module reimplements GEPA in TypeScript from the paper. See NOTICE.
